    <div class="lib-page-body">
      <div class="doc-page">

        <div class="doc-hero">
          <div class="doc-hero-logo">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" width="64" height="64" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect width="64" height="64" rx="14" ry="14" fill="#0a84ff"/>
              <path d="M18 48 L18 28 Q18 22 25 22 Q32 22 32 28 L32 48 M32 28 Q32 22 39 22 Q46 22 46 28 L46 48"
                    fill="none" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width="5"
                    stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-hero-tagline">Coding became Chatting</div>
        </div>

        <h1>What is meeEL</h1>
        <p>
          meeEL is a simple language. You write plain English. meeEL turns it into real code
          that runs on any device.
        </p>

        <p>
          You write <strong>one</strong> meeEL file. meeEL makes <strong>four</strong> files:
        </p>

        <table class="doc-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>From meeEL</th><th>What you get</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>home.html</code></td><td>The page structure</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>home.css</code></td><td>Colors and sizes</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>home.js</code></td><td>The click actions</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>server.py</code></td><td>A small server</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2>Only three symbols</h2>
        <p>meeEL has only three symbols:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>-</code> joins words in a name</li>
          <li><code>[ ]</code> holds a value</li>
          <li><code>#</code> marks a note (meeEL will not read it)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Nothing else. No semicolons. No brackets outside of values.</p>

        <h2>Why we built it</h2>
        <p>
          HTML, CSS, JavaScript and Python are powerful — but they have a steep learning curve.
          A 12-year-old with an idea cannot build a site without months of study.
        </p>
        <p>
          meeEL gives them the same power with the simplest possible syntax. The name of every
          block says what it does. There are no cryptic shortcuts. No jargon.
        </p>

        <h2>The seven libraries</h2>
        <p>Everything you need is a tap away — inside the Tools drawer:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Blocks</strong> — 152 building blocks (pages, cards, forms, tables)</li>
          <li><strong>Actions</strong> — 112 things your app can do (show, hide, fetch, beep)</li>
          <li><strong>Properties</strong> — 129 settings (colors, sizes, shadows)</li>
          <li><strong>Tokens</strong> — 145 style words (bold, round, hidden)</li>
          <li><strong>Fonts</strong> — 106 typefaces ready to use</li>
          <li><strong>Colors</strong> — 100 named colors plus a picker</li>
          <li><strong>Icons</strong> — 132 built-in icons</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What meeEL can do</h2>
        <p>
          Landing pages, portfolios, dashboards, restaurant menus, forms, quiz apps,
          to-do lists, calculators, dark-mode sites, multi-page sites, and installable apps.
        </p>

        <h2>What meeEL cannot do</h2>
        <p>
          meeEL is a frontend language. It does not store data, handle accounts, or process
          payments. There is no database, no login system, no backend by design.
        </p>
        <p>
          But meeEL can talk to any backend — Supabase, Firebase, MongoDB, or your own server —
          using the <code>bring</code> and <code>bring-json</code> actions.
        </p>

        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          No account. No login. Your code stays in your browser. meeEL never sends anything
          to a server.
        </p>

        <div class="doc-footer">
          <div class="doc-footer-brand">mee Innovations</div>
          <div class="doc-footer-links">
            <a href="https://meeel-page.onrender.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">meeel-page.onrender.com</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/meeEL-Code/meeel-engine" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/meeEL-Code/meeel-engine</a>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-footer-tagline">A language through which you can create and build everything you need.</div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

