    <div class="lib-page-body">
      <div class="doc-page">

        <h1>How to Publish</h1>
        <p>
          When your meeEL code is ready, tap the blue <strong>Download</strong> button at the
          top right. Choose <strong>Download as ZIP</strong> — meeEL gives you all files
          packed together.
        </p>

        <div class="doc-highlight">
          <strong>One meeEL file → four files</strong><br/>
          Your <code>.meeel</code> code becomes real HTML, CSS, JavaScript and a Python server.
        </div>

        <h2>Step 1 — Download your ZIP</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Tap the blue <strong>Download</strong> button at the top right.</li>
          <li>Choose <strong>Download as ZIP</strong>.</li>
          <li>You will get a file called <code>meeEL-Codes.zip</code>.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>The ZIP contains:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>home.html</code> — your page structure</li>
          <li><code>home.css</code> — colors and sizes</li>
          <li><code>home.js</code> — click actions</li>
          <li><code>home.meeel</code> — your original code</li>
          <li><code>server.py</code> — a small Python server</li>
          <li><code>README.md</code> — full guide</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Step 2 — See it on your own computer</h2>
        <p>
          Unzip the file. Inside the folder, just <strong>double-click</strong>
          <code>home.html</code> — it opens in your browser. That is your site, running
          on your device.
        </p>
        <p>If you want the small Python server:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Open a terminal in the folder.</li>
          <li>Run: <code>python server.py</code></li>
          <li>Your browser opens at <code>http://localhost:8000</code></li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Step 3 — Put it on the internet</h2>
        <p>
          You can host your site for free. Here are three easy options:
        </p>

        <h3>Option A — Render (recommended)</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Create a free account at <code>render.com</code></li>
          <li>Create a new <strong>Static Site</strong>.</li>
          <li>Connect your GitHub repo — or drag your ZIP.</li>
          <li>Render gives you a live URL. Done.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Option B — Netlify</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Go to <code>netlify.com/drop</code></li>
          <li>Drag your unzipped folder onto the page.</li>
          <li>Your site is live in 10 seconds.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Option C — GitHub Pages</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Create a GitHub repo.</li>
          <li>Upload the unzipped files.</li>
          <li>Settings → Pages → Source: main branch.</li>
          <li>Your site appears at <code>yourname.github.io/repo</code></li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Step 4 — Install as a phone app</h2>
        <p>
          meeEL sites work like phone apps. Open your live site on your phone:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Android (Chrome):</strong> tap the ⋮ menu → "Install app"</li>
          <li><strong>iPhone (Safari):</strong> tap Share → "Add to Home Screen"</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Your site now sits on the home screen like a real app. It works offline too.</p>

        <h2>About your API keys</h2>
        <p>
          If you used <code>connections-[...]</code> to store a Supabase or Firebase key,
          meeEL separates those from your code and puts them in a
          <code>.env</code> file. Your real key never goes into the HTML or JavaScript.
        </p>
        <div class="doc-warning">
          <strong>Never</strong> put a service-role key or private key into a public site.
          Only publishable keys belong in the browser. meeEL warns you about this in the
          Download panel.
        </div>

        <h2>Need help?</h2>
        <p>
          Open the <strong>Learn to write</strong> book inside the Tools drawer — it walks
          through everything chapter by chapter, in English and বাংলা.
        </p>

        <div class="doc-footer">
          <div class="doc-footer-brand">mee Innovations</div>
          <div class="doc-footer-tagline">Happy building.</div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script type="module" src="/src/ui/app.ts"></script>
